import Bitcoin.Activation.Bip9

/-!
# Y14 property-test corpus — Flags/Bip9 (BLK-073..081 state machine)

2026-10-16.

Ground truth: Bitcoin Core `src/versionbits.cpp:26-117` (GetStateFor),
`src/deploymentstatus.h` (query convention) and `src/versionbits_impl.h`
(Condition) @ pinned commit `cce32b1682d86076ee71c10f9788c48d44458a263`
(verified local checkout, `git rev-parse HEAD`), NOT the Lean code.
Generated by a python3 reference (seed 20261016, fully reproducible).
The reference contains TWO independent implementations of the BIP9 machine — a literal transliteration of Core's GetStateFor
(align / walk-back cache cut / forward transitions, count test :93 BEFORE
timeout test :95) and a BIP9-text forward boundary simulation — which are
cross-checked to agree on EVERY case before emission.

Time->height abstraction (the one the Lean interface documents): MTP(b) ↦ b;
nStartTime ↦ `start`; nTimeTimeout ↦ `deadline = start + timeoutPeriods *
period`; `count` is the abstracted aggregate of versionbits.cpp:84-92 over
the period ending at the boundary height (piecewise-constant stimulus).
Query semantics: `bip9State P h` ≡ Core `GetStateFor(pindexPrev = block at
height h)`; alignment identity hand-derived and case-verified:
aligned ancestor of H = period*⌊(H+1)/period⌋ − 1, nullptr (⇒ DEFINED) when
H+1 < period.

All assertion targets are the python oracle; every case is kernel
`decide`-checkable (recursion depth (h+1)/period kept ≤ ~65).

123 cases: 99 machine cases (B..G + random R) +
8 sentinel/wrapper cases (A) + 16 signal-predicate cases (I).
-/

namespace BitcoinProofs.Property.Y14.Bip9Corpus

open Bitcoin.Activation

set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000

/-! ## A. Sentinel wrappers via the public `thresholdState` entry point -/
-- A01: ALWAYS_ACTIVE start => ACTIVE (versionbits.cpp:35-37)
theorem case_a01 : thresholdState 4294967295 12345 2 4 (fun A => if A < 10 then 9 else 3 : UInt32 → UInt32) 0 = .active := by decide
-- A02: ALWAYS_ACTIVE even at genesis
theorem case_a02 : thresholdState 4294967295 0 0 1 (fun A => if A < 10 then 9 else 3 : UInt32 → UInt32) 0 = .active := by decide
-- A03: NEVER_ACTIVE start => FAILED (versionbits.cpp:40-42)
theorem case_a03 : thresholdState 4294967294 4294967295 1815 2016 (fun A => if A < 10 then 9 else 3 : UInt32 → UInt32) 4294967295 = .failed := by decide
-- A04: mainnet testdummy row: dormant at height 0
theorem case_a04 : thresholdState 4294967294 4294967295 1815 2016 (fun A => if A < 10 then 9 else 3 : UInt32 → UInt32) 0 = .failed := by decide
-- A05: mainnet testdummy row: dormant far in the future
theorem case_a05 : thresholdState 4294967294 4294967295 1815 2016 (fun A => if A < 10 then 9 else 3 : UInt32 → UInt32) 1000000 = .failed := by decide
-- A06: NEVER_ACTIVE beats an always-signalling count
theorem case_a06 : thresholdState 4294967294 1000 1 2 (fun A => if A < 10 then 9 else 3 : UInt32 → UInt32) 500 = .failed := by decide
-- A07: huge non-sentinel start: pre-start => defined forever
theorem case_a07 : thresholdState 4294960000 4294967000 1 2016 (fun A => if A < 10 then 9 else 3 : UInt32 → UInt32) 10000 = .defined := by decide
-- A08: huge non-sentinel start: still defined just below it
theorem case_a08 : thresholdState 4294960000 4294967000 1 2016 (fun A => if A < 10 then 9 else 3 : UInt32 → UInt32) 4294950000 = .defined := by decide

